{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And the servant took.</b> The authority was in his hand, since 'all the good of his master was in his hand.'" "<b>Ten camels.</b> To seat ten men upon them, to recite the blessings of betrothal and marriage." "<b>Of his master's camels.</b> From the choicest of them, from those raised in his household." "<b>And all the good of his master in his hand.</b> One may say that it is missing a mem, and it attaches to the mem of <b>מגמלי</b> — the meaning being 'and from all the good of his master' together with the ten camels, as it is written: 'vessels of silver and vessels of gold and delicacies.' And all this in order to draw to himself the hearts of those who saw him."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:05:32.713463263Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}